2172 0 obj
<<
/A 4019 0 R
/Alt (visualizes the network graphs of individuals' protest participation patterns in different protest episodes in all six case countries. Protest episodes are shown as labelled texts, with the text describing the protest issue \(see Appendix Part II\). Protesters are shown as either triangles, circles, diamonds, or squares, each shape also corresponding to a unique color. The legend shows that each shape and color corresponds to a network position inhibited by the individual protester: Diamonds for Boundary Spanners, Squares for Coordinators, Triangles for Both, and Circles for Pendants \(Non-Brokerage Positions\).)
/K 10
/P 54 0 R
/Pg 46 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
